      "math_academy_id": "q-5428",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence that has a $17$th term of $99$ and a common difference of $4.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since ${a}_{17}=99$ is $16$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{17} & ={a}_{1}+16d \\\\ 99 & ={a}_{1}+16(4) \\\\ 99 & ={a}_{1}+64 \\\\ 35 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =35+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =35+4n-4 \\\\  & =31+4n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
